    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin helps you display your Flickr photos and albums directly on your website. Built with PHP API integration and Bootstrap responsive CSS, it works smoothly across all devices and screen sizes.</p>\n<p><strong>View Pro Demo</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://awplife.com/demo/flickr-gallery-premium/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Flickr Gallery Premium</a></strong><br />\n<strong>Learn More About Pro:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://awplife.com/wordpress-plugins/flickr-gallery-wordpress-plugin/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Flickr Gallery Premium Features</a></strong><br />\n<strong>Where To Buy:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://awplife.com/account/signup/flickr-gallery-premium/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Buy Flickr Gallery Premium</a></strong></p>\n<p>You can showcase your Flickr photostream, albums, and profile on any page, post, or sidebar widget using simple shortcodes. The setup process takes just a few minutes.</p>\n<p><strong>Video Tutorial</strong></p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"How To Add Flickr Gallery On WordPress Website - Album Gallery Photostream Profile For Flickr\" width=\"750\" height=\"422\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/6X-u_9l9B9k?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>\n<p><strong>Getting Started</strong></p>\n<p>To start using the plugin, you need your <strong><a href=\"https://awplife.com/how-to-get-your-user-id-of-flickr/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Flickr User ID</a></strong> and <strong><a href=\"https://awplife.com/how-to-get-your-api-key-of-flickr/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Flickr API Key</a></strong>. Add these in the API Settings page, create your gallery, and paste the shortcode wherever you want it to appear.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Flickr currently allows API key creation only for Flickr Pro subscribers.</p>\n<h3>Free Version Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Display Flickr Photostream on your site</li>\n<li>Show Flickr Albums and collections</li>\n<li>Responsive gallery design for all devices</li>\n<li>Widget support for sidebars and footers</li>\n<li>Shortcode support for pages and posts</li>\n<li>Column layout settings (desktops, tablets, mobiles)</li>\n<li>Built-in lightbox for image viewing</li>\n<li>Image border and styling options</li>\n<li>Center and responsive image alignment</li>\n<li>Easy copy shortcode functionality</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Pro Version Features</h3>\n<p>Upgrade to Pro for additional features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Responsive profile header with follow button</li>\n<li>Fetch and display private Flickr photos</li>\n<li>Display videos from your Flickr photostream</li>\n<li>Justified gallery layout option</li>\n<li>Pagination settings for large galleries</li>\n<li>Photo limit up to 500 images</li>\n<li>30+ hover effects for albums and photostream</li>\n<li>Multiple lightbox styles with transition effects</li>\n<li>Custom CSS field for styling</li>\n<li>Multiple galleries on same page with slideshow</li>\n<li>Different lightbox image sizing options</li>\n<li>Color customization for lightbox title and icons</li>\n<li>Shadow and glow effects for thumbnails</li>\n<li>2D transition effects</li>\n<li>Gallery title and post settings</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Install the plugin via WordPress.org plugin directory or upload the files to your server.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the Plugins menu.</li>\n<li>Go to Flickr Gallery <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> API Settings.</li>\n<li>Enter your Flickr User ID and API Key.</li>\n<li>Go to Flickr Gallery <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Add Flickr Gallery.</li>\n<li>Configure your gallery settings and save.</li>\n<li>Copy the shortcode and paste it into any page, post, or widget.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20get%20my%20flickr%20user%20id%3F'>\nHow do I get my Flickr User ID?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Visit <a href=\"https://awplife.com/how-to-get-your-user-id-of-flickr/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">this guide</a> that shows you step-by-step how to find your Flickr User ID from your Flickr profile.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20create%20a%20flickr%20api%20key%3F'>\nHow do I create a Flickr API Key?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Follow <a href=\"https://awplife.com/how-to-get-your-api-key-of-flickr/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">this tutorial</a> to create your API key. Note that currently only Flickr Pro subscribers can create API keys.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='can%20i%20display%20multiple%20albums%20on%20one%20page%3F'>\nCan I display multiple albums on one page?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, you can create multiple galleries and place their shortcodes on the same page. Each gallery can show a different album from your Flickr account.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='does%20this%20plugin%20work%20with%20elementor%20or%20gutenberg%3F'>\nDoes this plugin work with Elementor or Gutenberg?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, the plugin generates shortcodes that work with any page builder including Elementor, Gutenberg, and classic editor.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='why%20are%20my%20photos%20not%20loading%3F'>\nWhy are my photos not loading?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Check that your User ID and API Key are entered correctly in the API Settings page. Also verify that your Flickr photos are set to public visibility.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='can%20i%20display%20private%20flickr%20photos%3F'>\nCan I display private Flickr photos?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The free version only displays public photos. The Pro version includes support for fetching and displaying private photos.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20add%20the%20gallery%20to%20a%20widget%3F'>\nHow do I add the gallery to a widget?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Go to Appearance <span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-exclude-emoji\">→</span> Widgets, add a Text widget to your sidebar, and paste your gallery shortcode inside it.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='is%20this%20plugin%20mobile%20responsive%3F'>\nIs this plugin mobile responsive?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, the gallery is fully responsive and adjusts automatically to different screen sizes including desktops, tablets, and mobile phones.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='what%20image%20sizes%20are%20supported%20in%20the%20lightbox%3F'>\nWhat image sizes are supported in the lightbox?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The plugin supports multiple image sizes for lightbox preview. You can configure the thumbnail and lightbox image sizes in the gallery settings.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20customize%20the%20gallery%20appearance%3F'>\nHow do I customize the gallery appearance?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Use the gallery settings to adjust columns, borders, and layout. For advanced customization, the Pro version includes a custom CSS field.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='where%20can%20i%20get%20support%3F'>\nWhere can I get support?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>For questions or issues, please visit the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/support/plugin/wp-flickr-gallery/\" rel=\"ugc\">plugin support forum</a>.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.5.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.9</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.5.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.8.3</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.9</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.8</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.8</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.7.2</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed Twenty Twenty-Five theme conflict</li>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.7.1</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.7.1</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.6.2</li>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.6.2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.6.1</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.5.4</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Bug fixes</li>\n<li>Tested with WordPress 6.5.2</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Display your Flickr albums, photostream, and photos on any page or widget. Responsive and easy to set up using Flickr API.",
